  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Home-Grown School Feeding in displacement affected communities of Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The project proposed by the World Food Programme (WFP) envisages to implement a Home-Grown School Feeding (HGSF) programme in selected areas of Sudan, specifically in the states of Gedaref, Kassala, Northern, and Red Sea. The primary objective of this programme is to improve education outcomes, nutrition status of children, livelihoods, and employment opportunities for women and youths.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A total o&lt;strong&gt;f 207,992 children, including 97,756 boys and 110,236 g&lt;/strong&gt;irls, are expected to benefit from this programme. The initiative also aims to create job opportunities, contribute to social protection activities, and empower women by involving them as suppliers of fresh foods.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The project will be implemented over a period of 48 months, with a total budget of EUR 32.27 million, of which EUR 30 million will be contributed by the EU. The programme will have a direct and lasting impact on its beneficiaries, including primary school children, smallholder farmers, and their families, communities, teachers, and local authorities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The HGSF programme will be implemented in various localities, including Al Qureisha, Basundah Galabat Ash-Shargiah, Hamashkoreib, North Delta, Rural Aroma, Telkok, Khashm Ghirba, Wad El Helew, West Kassala, Agig, Haiya, Jabiet Al Maadin, Sinkat, Tokar, Dongola, Delgo, and Halfa.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The lead organisation for this project is the World Food Programme, and the management mode will be indirect.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Overall, the project aims to support farming communities in improving their food security while motivating their children to go back to school and learn&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;quill-better-table-wrapper&quot;&gt;&lt;table class=&quot;quill-better-table&quot;&gt;&lt;colgroup&gt;&lt;col width=&quot;1005&quot;&gt;&lt;/colgroup&gt;&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr data-row=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;td data-row=&quot;1&quot; rowspan=&quot;1&quot; colspan=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;qlbt-cell-line&quot; data-row=&quot;1&quot; data-cell=&quot;1&quot; data-rowspan=&quot;1&quot; data-colspan=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country: Sudan &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;qlbt-cell-line&quot; data-row=&quot;1&quot; data-cell=&quot;1&quot; data-rowspan=&quot;1&quot; data-colspan=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;States:&lt;/strong&gt; Gedaref, Kassala, &lt;span style=&quot;background-color: white;&quot;&gt;Red Sea and Northern State&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;qlbt-cell-line&quot; data-row=&quot;1&quot; data-cell=&quot;1&quot; data-rowspan=&quot;1&quot; data-colspan=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Localities&lt;/strong&gt;: Al Qureisha, Basundah Galabat Ash-Shargiah, Hamashkoreib, North Delta, Rural Aroma, Telkok, Khashm Ghirba, Wad El Helew, West Kassala, Agig, Haiya, Jabiet Al Maadin, Sinkat, Tokar, Dongola, Delgo, Halfa&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr data-row=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;td data-row=&quot;2&quot; rowspan=&quot;1&quot; colspan=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;qlbt-cell-line&quot; data-row=&quot;2&quot; data-cell=&quot;1&quot; data-rowspan=&quot;1&quot; data-colspan=&quot;1&quot;&gt;48 months (as of the starting date of the implementation period)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr data-row=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;td data-row=&quot;3&quot; rowspan=&quot;1&quot; colspan=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;qlbt-cell-line&quot; data-row=&quot;3&quot; data-cell=&quot;1&quot; data-rowspan=&quot;1&quot; data-colspan=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr data-row=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;td data-row=&quot;4&quot; rowspan=&quot;1&quot; colspan=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;qlbt-cell-line&quot; data-row=&quot;4&quot; data-cell=&quot;1&quot; data-rowspan=&quot;1&quot; data-colspan=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EUR 30 million&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
